lanning any  further announcements uh this week uh  you know i want people to uh to despite  the the caution that we're all taking  the sensible caution you know people  should enjoy their christmases with  their families and friends of course  remain cautious and we will keep the  situation under review  even if the variant isn't the threat  that many had feared based on its  mutations scientists warn we may not be  so fortunate next time viruses are not  really  intending to damage their host they just  want to replicate and transmit and we  now see there's a paradigm or a  mechanism for the virus to fulfill all  of its evolutionary needs uh without  harming us to this to a similar degree  but of course the next variant that  arises may not may not do this it may be  completely different and therefore the  strategies for vaccination infection  control really needs to be considered  carefully so today  the uk health security agency also found  the effect of the booster is already  beginning to wane with protection  against symptomatic disease dropping by  15 to 25  10 weeks after having the jab it says  protection against serious disease is  likely to hold up for longer and there  are no signs yet that the uk needs to  follow israel in giving people a fourth  dose  thomas more sky news
 

